,-12,156.236,206.90003)\" fill=\"#23384a\"/>\n<use xlink:href=\"#font_2_18\" transform=\"matrix(12,0,0,-12,304.564,206.90003)\" fill=\"#23384a\"/>\n<use xlink:href=\"#font_2_23\" transform=\"matrix(12,0,0,-12,432.896,206.90003)\" fill=\"#23384a\"/>\n<use xlink:href=\"#font_2_1\" transform=\"matrix(12,0,0,-12,439.568,206.90003)\" fill=\"#23384a\"/>\n</g>\n</svg>\n","8 · 8 6 · 3 8 1 6"],["heading","HOW TO READ THE DIAGRAM"],["text","1. The leaves are the original input [3,8,1,6]."],["text","2. Combine each pair by taking its maximum: 8 and 6."],["text","3. Combine the two results to get 8. Read this diagram from bottom to top."],["heading","INTERVIEW MEMORY TIP"],["text","Divide into smaller problems, solve them, then combine results."]]